IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `types`
IMPORT `chapter-2-explanations`
IMPORT `chapter-4-exceptions`
IMPORT `chapter-4a-private-defence`
IMPORT `chapter-5-abetment`

§ `Chapter 18 -- Currency and bank notes`

-- Penal Code 1871 ss 489A, 489B, 489C, 489D, 489E, 489F, 489G, 489H, 489I.
-- Source: registers/source-bundle/PC1871.txt.
--
-- Nine sections that replaced the old Chapter 12 coin offences in 2019. They fall into
-- two families. ss 489A to 489E are about FORGED OR COUNTERFEIT currency: making it,
-- dealing in it, possessing it, making the tools for it, and abetting its making
-- abroad. ss 489F to 489I are about GENUINE currency that has been ALTERED: clipping
-- or adulterating a coin, changing the appearance of currency so it passes as a
-- different description, and passing on or possessing currency so altered.
--
-- s 489A(2) defines "bank note", "coin" and "currency" for all nine. Each is carried as
-- one fact so that a caller asserts which the thing is; the definitions are in the
-- field names. "Currency" is an inclusive definition ("includes any currency note or
-- coin ... which is legal tender"), so the fact is worded inclusively too.
--
-- PUNISHMENT IS NOT COMPUTED. Every section here carries its own sentence, and none is
-- decided.

§§ `Section 489A(2) -- Currency, bank note and coin`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 489A(2)"
GIVEN c IS A Currency
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the thing is currency or a bank note` IF
        c's `the thing is currency including a currency note or coin which is legal tender in the country or territory in which it is issued`
    OR  c's `the thing is a bank note being a promissory note or engagement for the payment of money to bearer on demand issued by a person carrying on the business of banking in any part of the world or issued by or under the authority of the government of any country or territory and intended to be used as equivalent to or as a substitute for money`

§§ `Sections 489A to 489D -- Forged or counterfeit currency`

-- s 489A: forging or counterfeiting, or knowingly performing any part of the process.
-- s 489B: delivering, selling, buying, receiving, importing, exporting, trafficking in
--   or using as genuine, knowing or having reason to believe it forged or counterfeit.
-- s 489C: possession with that knowledge, and intending to use it as genuine or that
--   it may be so used.
-- s 489D: making, mending, dealing in or possessing a die, machinery, instrument or
--   material for the purpose of being used, or knowing or having reason to believe it
--   is intended to be used, for forging or counterfeiting currency. No forged currency
--   need exist.
--
-- ss 489B and 489C each need the thing to BE forged or counterfeit, as well as the
-- knowledge of it: "any forged or counterfeit currency or bank note, knowing ..."

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 489A"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes forging or counterfeiting currency or a bank note under Penal Code 1871 section 489A
GIVEN c IS A Currency @desc Forging or counterfeiting currency or a bank note, or knowingly performing any part of the process.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes forging or counterfeiting currency` IF
        `the thing is currency or a bank note` c
    AND c's `forges or counterfeits or knowingly performs any part of the process of forging or counterfeiting the currency or bank note`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 489B"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes dealing in or using as genuine forged or counterfeit currency under Penal Code 1871 section 489B
GIVEN c IS A Currency @desc Delivering, selling, buying, receiving, importing, exporting, trafficking in or using as genuine forged or counterfeit currency or a bank note, knowing or having reason to believe it to be forged or counterfeit.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes using or trafficking in counterfeit currency` IF
        `the thing is currency or a bank note` c
    AND c's `the currency or bank note is forged or counterfeit`
    AND c's `delivers or sells to or buys or receives from any other person or otherwise imports exports or traffics in or uses as genuine the currency or bank note`
    AND c's `knows or has reason to believe the currency or bank note to be forged or counterfeit`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 489C"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes possession of forged or counterfeit currency under Penal Code 1871 section 489C
GIVEN c IS A Currency @desc Possession of forged or counterfeit currency or a bank note, knowing or having reason to believe it to be so and intending that it be used as genuine.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes possession of counterfeit currency` IF
        `the thing is currency or a bank note` c
    AND c's `the currency or bank note is forged or counterfeit`
    AND c's `has the currency or bank note in his possession`
    AND c's `knows or has reason to believe the currency or bank note to be forged or counterfeit`
    AND c's `intends to use the currency or bank note as genuine or that it may be used as genuine`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 489D"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes making or possessing instruments or materials for forging or counterfeiting currency under Penal Code 1871 section 489D
GIVEN c IS A Currency @desc Making, mending, dealing in or possessing any die, machinery, instrument or material for use, or known or believed to be intended for use, in forging or counterfeiting currency or bank notes.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes possessing instruments for counterfeiting currency` IF
        c's `makes mends or performs any part of the process of making or mending or buys sells or disposes of or has in his possession any die machinery instrument or material`
    AND c's `the die machinery instrument or material is for the purpose of being used or he knows or has reason to believe that it is intended to be used for forging or counterfeiting any currency or bank note`

§§ `Section 489E -- Abetting in Singapore the counterfeiting of currency out of Singapore`

-- A person within Singapore who abets the counterfeiting of currency out of Singapore
-- is punished as if he had abetted it within Singapore. The abetment is s 107 conduct,
-- taken from the Abetment record as s 111 takes it; the s 108 capable-person test is
-- not conjoined, because the section supplies the criminality of the thing abetted
-- itself. "Punished in the same manner" is punishment only.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 489E"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes abetting in Singapore the counterfeiting of currency out of Singapore under Penal Code 1871 section 489E
GIVEN c IS A Currency @desc The accused is within Singapore and the thing abetted is the counterfeiting of currency out of Singapore.
      ab IS AN Abetment @desc The s 107 abetment conduct -- instigation, conspiracy or intentional aiding.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes abetting the counterfeiting of currency abroad` c ab IF
        `the person abets the doing of a thing` ab
    AND c's `the accused is within Singapore`
    AND c's `the thing abetted is the counterfeiting of currency out of Singapore`

§§ `Sections 489F to 489I -- Altered currency`

-- s 489F: fraudulently or dishonestly performing on a COIN an operation that
--   diminishes its weight or alters its composition. The fault is s 24 or s 25. The
--   Explanation (scooping out part and filling the cavity alters the composition)
--   illustrates the operation and adds no limb.
-- s 489G: performing on any CURRENCY an operation that alters its appearance, with the
--   intention that it pass as currency of a different description. No fault element
--   beyond that intention.
-- s 489H: delivering as genuine, or as currency of a different description, or
--   attempting to induce a person to receive it as such, currency the accused knows or
--   has reason to believe has had a s 489F or s 489G operation performed on it. The
--   attempt is inside the section.
-- s 489I: possession of such currency, knowing or having reason to believe that a
--   s 489F or s 489G OFFENCE has been committed with respect to it, intending to use
--   it as genuine or that it may be so used.
--
-- Note the shift between ss 489H and 489I: s 489H asks whether an OPERATION mentioned
-- in the earlier sections has been performed; s 489I asks whether an OFFENCE under
-- them has been committed. They are two facts and are not merged. Neither is computed
-- from the s 489F or s 489G rule, because the operation may have been performed by
-- someone else whose facts this record does not carry.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 489F"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes fraudulently or dishonestly diminishing the weight or altering the composition of a coin under Penal Code 1871 section 489F
GIVEN c IS A Currency @desc Fraudulently or dishonestly performing on a coin an operation which diminishes its weight or alters its composition.
      f IS A Fault @desc Fault elements. The operation must be fraudulent (s 25) or dishonest (s 24).
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes diminishing or adulterating a coin` c f IF
        (`the act is done dishonestly` f OR `the act is done fraudulently` f)
    AND c's `the thing is a coin being metal used as money stamped and issued by or under the authority of the government of any country or territory in order to be so used`
    AND c's `performs on the coin an operation which diminishes its weight or alters its composition`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 489G"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes altering the appearance of currency so that it passes as currency of a different description under Penal Code 1871 section 489G
GIVEN c IS A Currency @desc Performing on currency an operation which alters its appearance, intending that it pass as currency of a different description.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes altering the appearance of currency` IF
        c's `the thing is currency including a currency note or coin which is legal tender in the country or territory in which it is issued`
    AND c's `performs on the currency an operation which alters its appearance`
    AND c's `intends that the currency will pass as currency of a different description`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 489H"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes delivering altered currency as genuine or as currency of a different description under Penal Code 1871 section 489H
GIVEN c IS A Currency @desc Delivering as genuine or as currency of a different description, or attempting to induce a person to so receive, currency known or believed to have had a s 489F or s 489G operation performed on it.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes delivering altered currency` IF
        c's `the thing is currency including a currency note or coin which is legal tender in the country or territory in which it is issued`
    AND c's `delivers to any other person as genuine or as currency of a different description from what it is or attempts to induce any person to receive as genuine or as currency of a different description the currency`
    AND c's `knows or has reason to believe that an operation mentioned in section 489F or 489G has been performed on the currency`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 489I"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes possession of altered currency with intent to use it as genuine under Penal Code 1871 section 489I
GIVEN c IS A Currency @desc Possession of currency known or believed to be the subject of a s 489F or s 489G offence, intending to use it as genuine or that it may be so used.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes possession of altered currency` IF
        c's `the thing is currency including a currency note or coin which is legal tender in the country or territory in which it is issued`
    AND c's `has the currency or bank note in his possession`
    AND c's `knows or has reason to believe that an offence under section 489F or 489G has been committed with respect to the currency`
    AND c's `intends to use the currency or bank note as genuine or that it may be used as genuine`

§§ `Proposed Act wrappers`

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes a counterfeit currency offence` IF
        (   `constitutes forging or counterfeiting currency` (a's `currency`)
         OR `constitutes using or trafficking in counterfeit currency` (a's `currency`)
         OR `constitutes possession of counterfeit currency` (a's `currency`)
         OR `constitutes possessing instruments for counterfeiting currency` (a's `currency`)
         OR `constitutes abetting the counterfeiting of currency abroad` (a's `currency`) (a's `abetment`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes an altered currency offence` IF
        (   `constitutes diminishing or adulterating a coin` (a's `currency`) (a's `fault`)
         OR `constitutes altering the appearance of currency` (a's `currency`)
         OR `constitutes delivering altered currency` (a's `currency`)
         OR `constitutes possession of altered currency` (a's `currency`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)
